# 4. MARKETPLACE COMMISSION

Boatly charges a commission only when a booking originates through the Boatly marketplace.

Example:

Customer searches on Boatly

↓

Customer books on Boatly

↓

Marketplace booking

↓

Boatly commission applies.

---

# 5. MANUAL BOOKINGS

Manual bookings are reservations entered by operators into the Boatly management system.

Examples:

* telephone booking
* WhatsApp booking
* walk-in customer
* returning customer
* direct website lead
* other offline/direct source

Boatly marketplace commission:

0%

This is a fundamental commercial principle.

The purpose is to encourage operators to place their entire reservation calendar inside Boatly.

Manual bookings still consume:

* fleet availability
* calendar slots
* CRM records
* analytics
* staff resources

but do not generate marketplace commission.

---

# 6. WHY MANUAL BOOKINGS ARE FREE OF COMMISSION

Charging commission on reservations Boatly did not generate would create an incentive for operators not to use the management platform.

Instead:

Direct reservation

↓

Operator enters it into Boatly

↓

0% marketplace commission

↓

Boatly calendar becomes accurate

↓

Marketplace availability becomes accurate

↓

Double bookings decrease

↓

Boatly marketplace improves

This creates a positive network effect.

---

