Transparent pricing can become an important positioning advantage.

A customer service fee may be introduced in the future only if:

* economics require it
* market testing supports it
* it is clearly disclosed before checkout

---

# 8. COMMISSIONABLE AMOUNT

Marketplace commission should apply to the commissionable booking subtotal.

Initial rule:

Commissionable:

* boat rental price
* Boatly-managed/operator-sold extras paid online where commercially applicable

Not commissionable by default:

* refundable security deposit
* taxes collected purely on behalf of authorities
* fuel paid directly at location
* offline charges outside Boatly
* refundable temporary authorizations

The final accounting/tax treatment will be validated during A9 and professional legal/accounting review.

---

# 9. COMPETITIVE POSITIONING

At the August 2026 planning date, public competitor information indicates marketplace owner commissions materially above Boatly's intended launch pricing.

Reference benchmarks checked during planning include:

* SamBoat: approximately 20% commission on rental price
* Click&Boat: commission can reach approximately 26%, subject to individual agreements

Boatly should initially position itself below large marketplace commission levels.

This is not a permanent guarantee.

Competitor pricing must be revalidated before commercial launch.

