# 33. OPERATOR CANCELLATION

Operator cancellations damage marketplace trust.

Recommended policy architecture:

First exceptional cancellation:

warning/review depending on reason.

Repeated unjustified cancellations may cause:

* ranking penalty
* temporary listing restriction
* operator suspension
* financial penalty where contractually/legal permitted

Customer must receive the applicable refund.

Boatly must preserve cancellation metrics for operator quality scoring.

Exact penalties will be finalized in commercial terms.

---

# 34. CUSTOMER CANCELLATION

Customer refund is determined by the cancellation policy snapshot stored in the booking.

Example:

€300 booking

Applicable policy allows 50% refund.

Customer receives:

€150

The economic allocation of the retained €150 must follow the contractual commercial rules.

Boatly commission should be calculated according to the final retained rental economics rather than blindly preserving commission on value returned to the customer.

Exact accounting implementation will be validated before production.

---

# 35. FULL REFUND

Where a booking is fully refunded:

the platform should not treat the original booking value as realized marketplace revenue.

Boatly's commission should normally reverse economically along with the refunded booking value, subject to:

* non-refundable provider processing costs
* operator cancellation responsibility
* contractual penalties
* exceptional dispute costs

---

# 36. PAYMENT PROCESSING COST AFTER REFUND

Payment providers may not return all original processing costs after a refund.

Therefore:

Customer refund

and

Boatly/operator economic settlement

are separate calculations.

Boatly must track:

* customer refund amount
* Boatly commission adjustment
* provider cost
* operator settlement adjustment

This prevents hidden financial losses.

---

# 37. OPERATOR PAYOUT POLICY

Recommended initial marketplace payout policy:

Customer pays at booking.

↓

Funds are processed securely.

↓

Booking takes place.

↓

Payout becomes eligible after the rental has successfully passed the defined payout-release point.

Initial commercial target:

approximately 24 hours after scheduled rental completion.

This can be adjusted depending on:

* Stripe Connect limitations
* fraud risk
* disputes
* cancellation windows
* operator history

Exact technical payout timing will be finalized during D5.

---

# 38. WHY NOT IMMEDIATE PAYOUT

Immediate payout at booking creates additional risk.

Example:

Customer books in May.

Rental happens in August.

Operator receives funds immediately.

Rental is cancelled in July.

Boatly must recover funds.

A delayed marketplace payout simplifies:

* cancellations
* fraud
* refunds
* operator failure
* disputes

However, operator cash-flow needs must be considered before final launch policy.

