# 66. A8 FINAL BUSINESS RULES

Initial Boatly commercial rules:

1. Marketplace bookings generate Boatly commission.

2. Manual bookings generate 0% marketplace commission.

3. Customer has no separate mandatory Boatly booking fee at launch.

4. Commission is configurable.

5. Commission is snapshotted on each booking.

6. Subscription plans can reduce marketplace commission.

7. Founding operators receive a temporary preferential pilot offer.

8. Security deposits are separate from marketplace revenue.

9. Payment-provider costs are tracked separately from Boatly commission.

10. Refunds adjust realized economic results.

11. Provider fees must not be mistaken for Boatly revenue.

12. Marketplace GMV and Managed Booking Volume are different metrics.

13. Historical financial terms are immutable.

14. Future enterprise agreements are supported.

15. Commercial rules must remain configuration-driven.

